# Quadra Competition Engine - example environment.
#
# The engine and its admin scripts read the shared data layer env at ../data/.env by
# default (override with DATA_ENV_PATH). The variables below are the ones the competition
# engine needs on top of what `npm run setup` already writes into ../data/.env. You can
# either add the missing ones to ../data/.env, or copy this file to .env and start the
# engine with DATA_ENV_PATH=./competition-engine/.env. The admin scripts also load a local
# .env automatically.
#
# Do NOT commit a real .env: COMPETITION_SECRET_KEY / DATA_SECRET_KEY are private keys.

# --- Required: on-chain identity (usually already in ../data/.env) ---
# The engine wallet that owns CompetitionCap and is the job_access::set_competition Seal
# reader. It signs every record_score / record_performance / release_prizes transaction.
COMPETITION_SECRET_KEY=suiprivkey1...
# Deployed quadra package + shared object ids (from `npm run setup` in data/).
QUADRA_PACKAGE_ID=0x...
AGENT_REGISTRY_ID=0x...
JOB_ACCESS_REGISTRY_ID=0x...
# Owned CompetitionCap id, written by `npm run capture-cap` (to COMPETITION_SECRET_KEY).
COMPETITION_CAP_ID=0x...

# --- Admin token (guards POST/PUT /competitions/:id/bind and the create script) ---
# COMPETITION_ADMIN_TOKEN takes precedence; ROLE_TOKEN_ADMIN is the shared fallback and is
# also what the template-seeding scripts use against the data gateway.
COMPETITION_ADMIN_TOKEN=change-me
ROLE_TOKEN_ADMIN=change-me

# --- Server ---
REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379
# HTTP + Socket.IO port. This is the value the web app points at via NEXT_PUBLIC_COMPETITION_URL.
COMPETITION_PORT=5100
# Reconcile + lifetime/end scan interval (ms).
COMPETITION_POLL_MS=3000
# Allowed clock skew on a signed agent socket handshake (ms).
COMPETITION_AUTH_WINDOW_MS=60000
# Browser origin allowed to read GET /competitions (the web app). Set this to your web
# origin in production (e.g. https://quadra.sh); defaults to * (open) for local dev.
COMPETITION_CORS_ORIGIN=*

# --- Evaluation engines (Walrus catalog) ---
# Eval engine URLs are stored in the data layer `eval_engines` database
# (POINTER_EVAL_ENGINES). Register after each enclave deploy:
#   cd ../data && EVALUATOR_ID=price-range-guess ENCLAVE_URL=http://localhost:5200 npm run register-eval-engine
# Deprecated local-dev override (merged on top of the catalog):
# EVAL_ENGINES={"price-range-guess":{"url":"http://localhost:5200"},"portfolio-roi":{"url":"http://localhost:5300"}}

# --- Network / RPC (shared with the data layer) ---
DATA_NETWORK=testnet
# Optional Sui JSON-RPC URL override (defaults to the public fullnode for DATA_NETWORK).
# DATA_BASE_URL=https://fullnode.testnet.sui.io:443
# Deployer key: used by `npm run capture-cap` (to transfer the cap) and as the
# release-prizes fallback signer when COMPETITION_SECRET_KEY is unset.
DATA_SECRET_KEY=suiprivkey1...

# --- Admin scripts only ---
# Where the create/bind/list scripts reach the running engine.
COMPETITION_URL=http://localhost:5100
# Data gateway, used by the template-seeding scripts (seed-template, seed-prediction-templates).
DATA_GATEWAY_URL=http://localhost:8787
# Optional: point the engine + scripts at a specific env file instead of ../data/.env.
# DATA_ENV_PATH=./competition-engine/.env
